WEBVTT

00:07.812 --> 00:10.564
Sh... Sorry.

00:10.919 --> 00:14.659
Do you got any dehydrated mango, ginger?

00:14.761 --> 00:16.527
Jicama, perhaps?

00:18.666 --> 00:19.865
Nah.

00:20.736 --> 00:24.671
Hmm.

00:24.773 --> 00:26.740
This place sucks.

00:32.776 --> 00:34.684
How much for that hat?

00:34.786 --> 00:36.953
And this?

00:38.378 --> 00:40.128
Ten dollars.

00:40.153 --> 00:42.694
Bet.

00:58.782 --> 01:02.719
Oh. Look at you.

01:25.577 --> 01:29.092
♪ Sweet little girl ♪

01:29.124 --> 01:33.250
♪ You know your baby loves you ♪

01:34.001 --> 01:38.669
♪ Your love is driving
me crazy, crazy, crazy ♪

01:38.711 --> 01:46.589
♪ Sweet little girl... ♪

01:56.006 --> 01:58.591
♪ Girl, I'm in love...

02:03.141 --> 02:04.207
Hello?

02:04.232 --> 02:06.867
Hey, yeah, um, I'm here for the pickup.

02:12.565 --> 02:14.837
Thank you.

02:54.060 --> 02:57.348
Wow. I should probably... yeah.

02:58.765 --> 03:00.866
Okay.

03:14.747 --> 03:16.685
Hello?

03:25.945 --> 03:27.696
Hello?

03:27.738 --> 03:30.781
Um, I'm here for the... the, uh, pick...

03:30.872 --> 03:32.772
Was that Mr. Wonder?

03:43.710 --> 03:44.978
In the car?

03:47.551 --> 03:50.086
Oh, yeah.

03:51.968 --> 03:53.875
Music of My Mind.

03:55.329 --> 03:56.702
Masterpiece.

03:56.805 --> 03:58.738
I love Stevie.

04:00.155 --> 04:01.178
Yeah, me, too.

04:01.203 --> 04:04.464
I-I like to, uh, listen
to it on long drives

04:04.496 --> 04:07.622
because, uh, his songs
are long, you know?

04:09.291 --> 04:11.765
Yes.

04:17.869 --> 04:19.267
I'm Darius.

04:20.024 --> 04:21.842
Apologies.

04:22.471 --> 04:24.479
I'm Theodore Perkins.

04:24.652 --> 04:28.321
Please... call me Teddy.

04:37.880 --> 04:40.964
Come on. Please, come sit in the parlor.

04:41.966 --> 04:47.295
Oh, cool. I've never been in
a house with a parlor before.

04:52.449 --> 04:55.184
Would you like a glass of water?

04:55.669 --> 04:57.006
Yeah.

04:57.031 --> 04:58.686
Kind of parched.

05:00.734 --> 05:03.778
Darius would like a glass of
water when you have a moment.

05:09.439 --> 05:11.381
Would you like some?

05:13.341 --> 05:14.407
What is that?

05:14.672 --> 05:17.312
It's a soft-boiled ostrich egg.

05:17.414 --> 05:19.006
It's called an owl's casket.

05:19.031 --> 05:20.798
Nah, I'm good.

06:12.279 --> 06:14.030
So...

06:17.215 --> 06:19.389
you're here about the piano.

06:19.644 --> 06:21.392
How did you hear about it?

06:23.099 --> 06:24.364
Um...

06:24.389 --> 06:27.560
someone posted on the
biohacking message board

06:27.574 --> 06:31.034
saying their boss had a
multicolored key piano.

06:31.055 --> 06:33.756
Trying to get rid of it. Free of charge.

06:34.226 --> 06:37.858
Sam. Was it Sam?

06:37.993 --> 06:40.411
My audiovisual woman.

06:40.433 --> 06:45.860
Uh, we don't use real names on
the message boards so, so maybe?

06:47.087 --> 06:49.786
Hmm. Oops.

06:53.860 --> 06:56.048
Are you a music lover?

06:57.493 --> 07:00.299
Yeah. Yeah, I consider myself... yeah.

07:00.402 --> 07:02.769
I work with a friend
of mine. He's a rapper.

07:02.871 --> 07:04.547
Rap.

07:05.841 --> 07:07.708
There's a funny one.

07:12.252 --> 07:15.669
I found it never quite
grew out of its adolescence.

07:17.149 --> 07:19.168
No, I wouldn't say that.

07:19.597 --> 07:21.823
You know, we got Jay-Z. He's, like, 65.

07:21.848 --> 07:25.146
But don't you find it
insufficient as an art form?

07:25.763 --> 07:28.935
Nah, I think, you know,
every now and again,

07:29.037 --> 07:31.404
people just want to have a good time.

07:32.721 --> 07:34.536
Good time.

07:36.814 --> 07:38.022
Hmm.

07:41.884 --> 07:43.635
How long have you played?

07:45.570 --> 07:47.349
Oh, you...

07:47.374 --> 07:48.436
you're talking about the piano.

07:48.461 --> 07:50.749
Uh, nah, I never studied.

07:50.774 --> 07:53.428
I just, uh, kind of
like the way it looks,

07:53.429 --> 07:55.764
especially this one
with the colored keys.

07:55.791 --> 07:58.225
Are you a fan of Benny's?

08:00.021 --> 08:00.986
Who?

08:02.945 --> 08:04.680
Benny Hope.

08:05.025 --> 08:06.982
The pianist.

08:07.084 --> 08:08.785
He's the one who owned the piano.

08:08.887 --> 08:10.289
He's my brother.

08:11.975 --> 08:15.056
Oh, sh-shit! Is that Keith Jarrett?

08:16.018 --> 08:16.977
Yes.

08:17.102 --> 08:18.769
- Let me look at that.
- Yes.

08:18.869 --> 08:21.206
And Stevie, as well.

08:21.231 --> 08:24.847
And Al Jarreau and Ahmad Jamal.

08:24.902 --> 08:26.844
I think Nina's over there somewhere.

08:26.937 --> 08:28.897
Ahmad and my brother,

08:29.143 --> 08:31.751
they had a residency
in New York together.

08:32.096 --> 08:34.627
Hmm. That's Flames, man.

08:34.666 --> 08:37.823
Yes. Flames.

08:39.483 --> 08:44.776
My-my brother and Ahmad,
they were staying at a-a hotel

08:44.902 --> 08:47.629
in Brooklyn off of Bergen Street.

08:47.654 --> 08:49.488
Eight dollars a night,
if you can believe it.

08:49.513 --> 08:51.942
He told me something I'll never forget.

08:52.044 --> 08:54.912
He said, "Your brother...

08:55.170 --> 08:59.313
plays pain better than anyone."

09:01.571 --> 09:03.906
Benny just played what he knew.

09:05.712 --> 09:09.597
Is he, uh, no longer with us?

09:10.487 --> 09:12.449
No, he's alive.

09:13.292 --> 09:15.572
He lives here with me.

09:16.854 --> 09:18.393
I take care of him.

09:18.418 --> 09:21.253
He developed a rare skin condition.

09:21.781 --> 09:24.416
Can no longer go in the sunlight.

09:28.651 --> 09:32.860
Yeah. You see, I keep
it quite dark in here.

09:32.962 --> 09:35.419
- Damn.
- Yeah.

09:35.933 --> 09:37.833
He must get depressed.

09:37.935 --> 09:39.702
It's not easy.

09:40.092 --> 09:41.425
But who knows?

09:42.065 --> 09:45.309
Maybe one day we'll get
a great album out of it.

09:46.622 --> 09:48.333
A masterpiece.

09:51.953 --> 09:54.086
Yeah. Righteous, brother.

09:54.425 --> 09:57.090
Uh, your, uh, your butler or whatever,

09:57.192 --> 09:59.694
they, um, didn't bring the water yet.

10:00.451 --> 10:02.697
Oh, I don't have a butler.

10:04.506 --> 10:06.802
I just use this to remember things.

10:08.139 --> 10:10.480
Finish that hat for Dionne Warwick.

10:10.505 --> 10:14.886
Wash your hands, immediately.

10:14.922 --> 10:16.923
Darius would like a glass of water

10:17.017 --> 10:19.474
when you have a moment.

10:19.558 --> 10:21.391
Right then.

10:23.826 --> 10:25.692
Excuse me.

10:41.388 --> 10:42.430
This...

10:57.183 --> 11:01.060
Yeah, I can't sit next to this. Mm-mm.

11:09.510 --> 11:11.035
Mm.

11:21.148 --> 11:22.858
Uh-huh.

11:48.390 --> 11:50.524
Oh.

13:01.256 --> 13:03.216
- Oh!
- Ooh!

13:07.718 --> 13:09.860
What are you doing up here?

13:09.884 --> 13:12.511
Uh, I-I just heard the piano.

13:12.550 --> 13:13.843
It sounded great, so...

13:13.868 --> 13:18.129
Shh, shh. Benny, he... he's sleeping.

13:18.591 --> 13:20.302
He's very tired, um...

13:20.825 --> 13:21.885
he needs his rest.

13:22.596 --> 13:24.097
- You know?
- Okay.

13:24.146 --> 13:26.467
- Uh-huh. Okay.
- Thank you.

13:26.492 --> 13:28.911
Um, cool.

13:28.936 --> 13:31.654
Do you... do you still want the water?

13:31.757 --> 13:32.822
Oh... yeah.

13:32.924 --> 13:34.792
I can bring it to you.

13:35.151 --> 13:37.051
Downstairs.

13:37.575 --> 13:39.576
Bottled or tap?

13:39.641 --> 13:42.344
Uh... bottled, I guess.

13:42.369 --> 13:43.904
Oh. Bottled.

13:45.434 --> 13:48.394
I'll bring it... I have Fiji, and Evian.

13:48.459 --> 13:50.745
I'll mix it with some Poland Springs.

13:50.847 --> 13:51.846
Maybe a Voss?

13:51.948 --> 13:54.146
Okay.

13:54.243 --> 13:55.342
No, I'll see you downstairs.

13:55.353 --> 13:57.145
But I just wanted to ask...

14:00.916 --> 14:02.083
Okay.

14:02.187 --> 14:03.367
Why the fuck you still there?

14:03.392 --> 14:06.873
Look, man, I really,
really want this piano, man.

14:06.898 --> 14:07.818
It's nice.

14:07.843 --> 14:10.578
There's colored keys. And it's free.

14:10.608 --> 14:12.817
But is you willing to
die for it, though, man?

14:12.920 --> 14:14.430
I mean, he sound like a serial killer.

14:14.455 --> 14:17.217
And let me get a five cheese
Krystal combo, no fries.

14:17.233 --> 14:18.276
It's cheaper with fries.

14:18.282 --> 14:19.158
No fries.

14:19.183 --> 14:20.950
That's rich nigga shit, man.

14:20.975 --> 14:22.531
You don't know nothing about that.

14:22.556 --> 14:25.297
Look, man, if I leave, I'll regret it.

14:25.444 --> 14:27.321
And I got a two regret life limit pact.

14:27.398 --> 14:29.064
Uh, wait, wait, wait, wait.

14:29.166 --> 14:30.266
A what?

14:30.837 --> 14:33.003
A two regret life limit pact.

14:33.246 --> 14:35.637
Somebody got to take
me out if I go over two.

14:35.747 --> 14:39.978
What? How would anyone know
you went over two regrets?

14:40.003 --> 14:41.036
I'd tell them.

14:41.670 --> 14:43.707
- Look...
- Oh, shit.

14:43.732 --> 14:44.951
Paper Boi!

14:45.053 --> 14:47.221
I mean, the dude is
obviously a weirdo, man.

14:47.323 --> 14:48.455
Look, now just play along with it,

14:48.557 --> 14:50.258
get the piano, get the hell up out.

14:50.360 --> 14:51.259
Yeah, but how, though, man?

14:51.361 --> 14:53.094
I feel like...

14:53.119 --> 14:55.154
like he stalling or something.

14:55.411 --> 14:57.110
Like he want to keep me here.

14:57.135 --> 14:58.022
Explain it again, man.

14:58.047 --> 14:59.763
Is Teddy the white
dude or the black dude?

14:59.788 --> 15:02.795
You know what? I don't even
think Teddy exists, bro.

15:02.820 --> 15:05.867
I feel like Benny created
Teddy to make up for the fact

15:05.914 --> 15:07.790
that he made himself look like a ghoul.

15:07.806 --> 15:08.805
A ghoul?

15:08.830 --> 15:10.183
I mean, how bad is it?

15:10.285 --> 15:11.951
It's real bad, man.

15:12.053 --> 15:13.532
I mean, bad.

15:13.579 --> 15:16.633
The nigga look like somebody
left Sammy Sosa in the dryer.

15:16.658 --> 15:18.260
Sammy Sosa?

15:18.729 --> 15:20.619
Yeah. Skin bleaching?

15:20.644 --> 15:22.497
Look, have somebody type in, um,

15:22.522 --> 15:24.542
"Sammy Sosa hat" in Google image search.

15:24.605 --> 15:25.784
Hey, man, look, man.

15:25.809 --> 15:27.958
Sometimes, people come
over, they want a quarter,

15:27.983 --> 15:29.573
and they feel like they
can sit and chat and shit.

15:29.598 --> 15:31.136
But other people, you
know what I'm saying, like,

15:31.161 --> 15:33.030
they want an eighth, they pay
me, and they get the hell on.

15:33.044 --> 15:35.004
- Can I take a flick? To Laurence.
- Look, man...

15:35.043 --> 15:36.617
- Say happy birthday, Laurence.
- That's how I know

15:36.629 --> 15:38.506
- that I'm simply a conduit...
- This nigga gonna stunt on me

15:38.534 --> 15:39.826
- with the new iPhone.
- between them and their weed.

15:39.851 --> 15:42.044
See, keep gunning, and
he ain't got no choice

15:42.069 --> 15:44.395
but to make clear what he want from you.

15:44.420 --> 15:46.537
I see what you're saying.
I see, I see what you're...

15:46.639 --> 15:48.628
you're saying be unequivocally honest

15:48.653 --> 15:50.675
to make a healthy transaction.

15:51.352 --> 15:52.551
Wow, man, you know what?

15:52.591 --> 15:54.717
You keep this up, you could
be the next Steve Harvey, bro.

15:54.816 --> 15:56.649
Steve Harvey, nigga? No, no, no.

15:56.751 --> 15:59.188
I'm-I'm like Dr. Phil,
you know what I'm saying?

15:59.213 --> 16:01.132
- Yo.
- Hell, that, that nigga stay caked up.

16:01.143 --> 16:02.791
- Yo! Shit!
- What the...?

16:02.893 --> 16:04.726
Oh, shit! Oh!

16:04.828 --> 16:06.495
- What happened?
- Yo!

16:07.799 --> 16:10.500
Yo, why this nigga the same
color as his fucking hat?

16:11.937 --> 16:14.672
Yeah, man, this nigga looks
like a white man's penis.

16:16.639 --> 16:17.558
Yo, man,

16:17.580 --> 16:20.379
why this nigga look like
what's under a scab, though?

16:22.818 --> 16:25.051
- Goddamn.
- Oh, God.

16:25.076 --> 16:26.200
Peace, man.

16:26.225 --> 16:27.190
All right, peace.

16:27.215 --> 16:28.214
Oh, God.

16:30.821 --> 16:32.328
Put some extra fries in there.

16:32.353 --> 16:33.321
Take them out.

16:33.346 --> 16:34.822
Just don't eat them, damn.

16:34.847 --> 16:36.847
Man.

16:37.379 --> 16:38.412
Hmm.

17:07.527 --> 17:08.486
Ugh.

17:08.604 --> 17:09.804
Surprise.

17:09.906 --> 17:14.576
Shit. Yeah, I'm not a big photo person.

17:14.795 --> 17:16.528
Apologies.

17:16.684 --> 17:19.091
Um, this is yours, anyway.

17:20.162 --> 17:21.652
I got you your water.

17:22.053 --> 17:24.398
Oh, yes, thank you.

17:24.405 --> 17:26.073
I needed that.

17:31.199 --> 17:32.658
Hmm.

17:33.534 --> 17:36.617
Oh. That's cool.

17:37.871 --> 17:40.519
Feel free to take any of it.

17:41.545 --> 17:43.145
Yeah.

17:47.805 --> 17:49.520
What is this place, man?

17:49.622 --> 17:50.922
It's a gift shop.

17:51.423 --> 17:55.527
I designed it myself to
feel... like a trophy room.

17:55.629 --> 17:58.038
More in the motif of the museum.

17:58.063 --> 18:00.421
Oh, wait, so you're turning
this whole place into a museum?

18:00.446 --> 18:03.198
Yes. I've already started the process

18:03.223 --> 18:05.324
of making this a historical site.

18:05.948 --> 18:08.557
You're actually the first
person to be in here.

18:08.737 --> 18:11.434
Feel free to Twitter
or blogspot any of it.

18:11.637 --> 18:14.300
Uh, you know what, actually,
I'm kind of in a rush, uh...

18:14.325 --> 18:17.455
May I show you something? Um...

18:17.557 --> 18:19.356
I-I promise to get you your piano.

18:19.381 --> 18:24.396
I... I really think you'll
like what I have in store.

18:27.170 --> 18:28.601
Sure.

18:35.215 --> 18:36.674
What's in there?

18:36.680 --> 18:37.949
Go ahead.

18:38.324 --> 18:40.341
Walk in.

18:44.013 --> 18:45.390
Okay.

18:49.608 --> 18:51.597
Hey, uh, Teddy?

18:51.957 --> 18:53.191
Uh...

18:54.265 --> 18:57.105
This is my favorite part of the museum.

18:58.078 --> 19:00.041
What the hell is this?

19:01.042 --> 19:02.808
This is my father.

19:04.053 --> 19:06.351
He's the reason for all of this.

19:07.758 --> 19:09.484
When me and Benny were children,

19:09.509 --> 19:12.312
he instituted a very
rigorous training method.

19:12.337 --> 19:14.357
Piano three hours a day,

19:14.382 --> 19:15.548
twice a day.

19:15.766 --> 19:17.567
With exams on Sundays,

19:18.105 --> 19:20.166
that, if failed,

19:21.957 --> 19:24.160
meant physical punishment.

19:25.937 --> 19:27.937
He wanted the best out of us.

19:31.318 --> 19:33.006
It's because of him we have all of this.

19:33.397 --> 19:36.106
So you said your dad,
uh, used to beat you

19:36.147 --> 19:37.372
so you'd be good at piano?

19:37.397 --> 19:38.756
To be good at life.

19:40.672 --> 19:42.350
We were his sacrifice.

19:43.287 --> 19:44.976
Oh. Well, um, I'm not trying

19:45.001 --> 19:46.837
to, like, shit on your
dad, or nothing, man,

19:46.862 --> 19:50.231
but that seems a little... unnecessary.

19:51.781 --> 19:54.042
Most people wouldn't understand.

19:54.993 --> 19:57.290
To make an omelet, you
have to break a few eggs.

19:58.278 --> 20:01.571
I mean, to build bridges,
people have to fall.

20:01.597 --> 20:03.025
Are you not mad at your dad?

20:03.050 --> 20:05.151
Of course not.

20:05.822 --> 20:08.782
There was no way for a child
to understand what was at stake.

20:09.155 --> 20:11.322
He just wanted the best for us.

20:12.979 --> 20:15.147
My father used to say,

20:15.804 --> 20:19.930
"Great things come from great pain."

20:23.826 --> 20:26.119
I want this wing of the museum

20:26.175 --> 20:28.653
to be dedicated to great fathers.

20:29.129 --> 20:32.308
My father, Joe Jackson,

20:32.333 --> 20:33.933
Marvin Gay Sr....

20:35.073 --> 20:36.744
Tiger Woods's father,

20:36.769 --> 20:38.764
Serena Williams's father,

20:40.038 --> 20:41.248
- _
- the father that drops off

20:41.249 --> 20:43.289
Emilio Estevez in The Breakfast Club.

20:43.313 --> 20:45.042
Hey, uh, look, I...

20:45.081 --> 20:46.415
I'd like to make this transaction

20:46.415 --> 20:48.543
as efficient as possible.

20:48.568 --> 20:51.682
So is there any documents I got to sign?

20:51.707 --> 20:53.274
For tax purposes?

20:56.459 --> 20:58.210
Of course.

21:18.422 --> 21:19.421
Uh...

21:19.587 --> 21:20.775
Ted?

21:21.275 --> 21:25.561
Sure, um, sorry I can't,
uh, thank Benny himself,

21:25.586 --> 21:26.898
personally, man.

21:26.923 --> 21:28.624
Don't be.

21:28.649 --> 21:31.476
The disease is very advanced,

21:31.501 --> 21:35.025
and he doesn't like
people seeing him that way.

21:36.961 --> 21:39.097
It's a very hard thing.

21:39.878 --> 21:40.945
Yeah.

21:41.477 --> 21:44.307
- I can imagine...
- No, you can't!

21:46.737 --> 21:48.947
You have no idea.

22:00.434 --> 22:03.060
Sign the highlighted parts.

22:06.036 --> 22:08.825
I have to go turn on the elevator.

22:09.592 --> 22:11.817
When it arrives,

22:11.842 --> 22:14.141
place the piano on it.

22:15.169 --> 22:16.659
I'll wait for you in the lobby.

22:16.684 --> 22:18.350
Okay, well, thanks...

22:29.107 --> 22:31.608
All right, what is this?

22:33.520 --> 22:34.656
The hell?

23:21.606 --> 23:23.652
Oh, no, no, no, no, no. Back.

23:41.397 --> 23:43.617
All right.

23:44.250 --> 23:46.804
Fine, destiny.

24:18.419 --> 24:20.171
Shh.

24:30.262 --> 24:32.638
_

24:37.025 --> 24:39.602
Okay. What do you want me to do?

24:50.267 --> 24:52.560
_

24:55.836 --> 24:58.508
Come on. Are you serious?

24:58.956 --> 24:59.922
Uh...

25:00.431 --> 25:03.051
But why can't, why can't
you just get the gun?

25:06.602 --> 25:09.441
All right. All right.
I'll go get your gun,

25:09.466 --> 25:11.460
but I got to put my piano
in the car first, okay?

25:11.485 --> 25:13.177
So you stay here.

25:13.202 --> 25:15.868
And I'll be back with your... gun.

25:30.611 --> 25:31.737
Why would he say that, though?

25:31.768 --> 25:34.968
I don't even know, bro.
This dude crazy, bruh.

25:36.059 --> 25:38.757
He want me to kill him,
this dude way past depressed.

25:38.782 --> 25:41.445
This whole situation's just been weird

25:41.470 --> 25:44.266
since I got here.

25:44.291 --> 25:46.143
Yep. Fuck this shit, bro.

25:46.198 --> 25:47.574
Look, I got the piano.

25:47.581 --> 25:49.884
Now I'm just gonna get
the hell up out of...

25:58.743 --> 26:00.869
Let me call you back, bro.

26:04.019 --> 26:06.052
Hey. Hey, Teddy!

26:06.765 --> 26:08.570
Your car is blocking mine.

26:23.541 --> 26:25.184
Teddy?

26:45.296 --> 26:47.881
Come on, Benny, put something into it.

26:50.965 --> 26:52.841
Posture.

26:53.423 --> 26:56.726
Posture. Keep your form.

26:59.913 --> 27:01.812
Don't you cry.

27:06.678 --> 27:08.429
Again!

27:09.265 --> 27:11.252
- I love this song.
- Oh, shit.

27:17.304 --> 27:18.222
Yeah.

27:19.164 --> 27:20.987
Something wrong?

27:22.284 --> 27:23.384
Uh...

27:23.409 --> 27:24.608
Watch your form.

27:24.633 --> 27:28.142
Yeah. You-you, uh, parked your
car right in front of mine.

27:28.681 --> 27:29.898
Oh.

27:33.030 --> 27:34.347
I'll move it.

27:36.532 --> 27:37.598
Um...

27:38.315 --> 27:40.382
Anything else?

27:40.541 --> 27:45.017
Uh, where's your, uh, bath-bathroom?

27:48.605 --> 27:50.732
It's up the stairs.

27:52.630 --> 27:54.515
Third door on your left.

27:56.648 --> 27:58.065
Okay.

27:59.723 --> 28:02.144
Right next to the attic.

28:03.693 --> 28:06.176
I was just up there myself.

28:08.110 --> 28:10.403
Do you know what I found?

28:14.479 --> 28:16.512
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

28:16.537 --> 28:18.615
Hey, man. Chill, chill.

28:18.640 --> 28:20.452
Congratulations.

28:22.116 --> 28:23.888
For-for what?

28:27.319 --> 28:29.120
I choose you.

28:30.061 --> 28:32.262
You're my sacrifice.

28:34.991 --> 28:37.158
Put your phone on the ground.

28:45.368 --> 28:46.619
No.

28:47.486 --> 28:49.056
Keep that.

28:50.300 --> 28:52.353
I want it to look real.

28:53.472 --> 28:55.276
Want what to look real?

28:55.301 --> 28:56.971
The home invasion.

28:57.204 --> 28:58.831
You killed Benny because
you were obsessed.

28:58.872 --> 29:00.122
No, man. You...

29:00.164 --> 29:02.319
Look, there is no
fucking Benny, all right?

29:02.344 --> 29:03.797
Exactly.

29:07.774 --> 29:09.337
Exactly.

29:13.338 --> 29:15.750
Sit in the chair.

29:34.464 --> 29:36.090
Put them on.

29:36.207 --> 29:37.771
Ankles first.

30:01.345 --> 30:04.222
You know, uh, not all great things

30:04.244 --> 30:06.528
come from great pain.

30:08.635 --> 30:10.502
Sometimes it's love.

30:10.527 --> 30:12.637
Not everything's a sacrifice.

30:14.474 --> 30:17.183
Sacrifices are necessary, Darius.

30:17.373 --> 30:19.441
Yeah, maybe.

30:22.682 --> 30:24.631
But your dad should have said sorry.

30:27.473 --> 30:29.256
I'm sorry.

30:30.672 --> 30:32.084
Shit.

30:33.274 --> 30:35.781
I went through daddy shit myself.

30:36.704 --> 30:38.821
But when you're young,
you try to just...

30:38.846 --> 30:41.475
make it be okay and say
everything's gonna be fine.

30:41.500 --> 30:42.326
And that's just,

30:42.351 --> 30:44.351
you don't know the difference, but...

30:45.055 --> 30:46.641
that don't give you an excuse to grow up

30:46.649 --> 30:49.609
and repeat the same shit over and over.

30:50.104 --> 30:53.908
It's like there's a,
there's a "what if" factor.

30:54.650 --> 30:57.142
What if you would have been
great at something else?

30:57.527 --> 30:59.736
Or if you would have seen the love...

31:01.207 --> 31:04.482
instead of all the other
shit like, like Stevie.

31:05.678 --> 31:07.621
I'm sorry?

31:08.081 --> 31:10.116
Stevie Wonder.

31:10.788 --> 31:14.380
Stevie had his own... sacrifices.

31:14.405 --> 31:16.035
He was blind.

31:16.060 --> 31:18.194
Yeah, but he wasn't blinded.

31:20.585 --> 31:22.639
He saw through his music.

31:24.414 --> 31:26.261
That's beautiful...

31:32.713 --> 31:34.481
but wrong.

31:47.878 --> 31:49.243
Benny.

31:50.498 --> 31:52.416
You're alive.

31:55.630 --> 31:56.562
Shit.

31:59.857 --> 32:01.037
Fuck.

32:07.150 --> 32:10.417
Benny, uh, look. I'm sorry that you

32:10.487 --> 32:12.688
had to go through what
you had to go through, man.

32:12.713 --> 32:13.893
It...

32:14.644 --> 32:15.881
What?

32:16.678 --> 32:18.146
Oh.

32:23.506 --> 32:25.507
Wait, Benny, what are
you, what are you do...?

32:25.632 --> 32:27.216
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

32:27.231 --> 32:29.191
Wait, wait, wait. Oh, shit!

32:29.216 --> 32:31.283
Oh! Fuck.

32:31.770 --> 32:34.605
Oh, shit. Goddamn it.

32:39.160 --> 32:40.993
Ugh.

32:41.174 --> 32:43.387
Fuck.

34:26.370 --> 34:28.955
Synced and corrected by Octavia
